Round gen_r5 complete. Both deliverables are in place: `impl/gen_dense_prime.c` (exact-tile GEMM rewrite, `GDP_MAP_SQRT` knob kept as a documented loser) and a new "Round gen_r5" section in `strategies/gen_dense_prime.md`. Everything was measured on the node holding one core lease with interleaved same-core A/Bs (the gen_batchlane r4 protocol), the shipped build is bit-identical to r4 at all 15 supported sizes (so zero numerics risk), and all three gates pass on the node with ≥17x margin. The main wins are on the generic class sizes: **L=17 −17%, L=19 −10%, L=23 −8%, L=20 −10%**, with L=31 at parity as intended (its kernels were already compile-time exact); the sqrt-map experiment lost everywhere (+16% at 31) and is recorded with numbers.

Exact-tile generic GEMM (full 4-zmm d-chunks + exact 1–3-zmm/1–3-column tails, bit-identical outputs); L=31 graded cell 119.89 µs/transform at B=16 and 121.60 µs at B=1 (17: 27.6, 19: 36.9, 23: 61.2, 20: 39.5); single-call rel L2 = 3.9e-16, two-step gate 1.7e-15.
